    "title": "Barcelona vs Rayo Vallecano Lineups, Predictions, Live Streaming, How & Where to Watch on TV",
    "text": "FC Barcelona will play at the Spotify Camp Nou for the third straight game in one week, but this time in La Liga against Rayo Vallecano.FC Barcelona is top of the La Liga table with 70 points after 28 league matches played. Rayo Vallecano is 13th in the league table with 32 points.AdvertisementLast weekend, Rayo Vallecano drew 1-1 with Levante in La Liga. During the week, Rayo Vallecano lost 1-0 to Samsunspor in the second leg of the UEFA Conference League Round of 16, but Rayo Vallecano advanced to the quarterfinals after winning 3-2 on aggregate.FC Barcelona defeated Sevilla 5-2 at home in La Liga last weekend to remain top of the league table. During the week, Barcelona defeated Newcastle United 7-2 in the Champions League Round of 16 second leg and won 8-3 on aggregate to reach the quarterfinals.Robert Lewandowski of FC Barcelona celebrates after scoring a goal with Lamine Yamal of FC Barcelona Gerard Martin of FC Barcelona Joao Cancelo of FC Barcelona during the UEFA Champions League 2025/26 Round of 16 Second Leg match between FC Barcelona and Newcastle United FC at Camp Nou on March 18, 2026 in Barcelona, Spain. (Photo by Xavi Bonilla/DeFodi Images/DeFodi via Getty Images)Photo by Xavi Bonilla/DeFodi Images/DeFodi via Getty Images (Photo by Xavi Bonilla&sol;DeFodi Images&sol;DeFodi via Getty Images)Earlier this season, Rayo Vallecano hosted FC Barcelona at the Estadio de Vallecas on August 31, 2025. The match finished in a 1-1 draw, with Lamine Yamal scoring a penalty kick and Fran Perez finding the equalizer.AdvertisementOfficial Lineups for FC Barcelona and Rayo VallecanoFC BarcelonaGoalkeeper: Joan GarciaDefenders: Joao Cancelo, Gerard Martin, Pau Cubarsi, Ronald AraujoMidfielders: Pedri, Marc Bernal, Fermin LopezForwards: Raphinha, Robert Lewandowski, Lamine YamalInjuries: Tonu Fernandez, Alejandro Balde, Andreas Christensen, Eric Garcia, Jofre Torrents, Jules Kounde, Frenkie De JongRayo VallecanoGoalkeeper: Augusto BatallaDefenders: Pep Chavarria, Pathe Ciss, Florian Lejeune, Andrei RatiuMidfielders: Pedro Diaz, Oscar Valentin, Gerard GumbauForwards: Fran Perez, Isi, Carlos MartinInjuries: Nobel Mendy* (*Suspended)FC Barcelona vs Rayo Vallecano will kick off at 9 a.m. ET/ 6 a.m. PT in the United States. The match will kick off at 2 p.m. local time at Spotify Camp Nou in Barcelona, Spain.AdvertisementThe match will be available to watch in the United States and Spain through select TV channels and streaming services.ESPN Select (USA)ESPN Unlimited (USA)ESPN Deportes (USA)Movistar (Spain)DAZN (Spain)LaLiga TV (Spain)Prediction: FC Barcelona 3-0 Rayo VallecanoThis story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Mar 22, 2026, where it first appeared in the Soccer section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
